                                                                  2428 1451
             New evaluation of chromium isotopes                  2428 1451
                 BNL, ORNL, IAEA - August 2020                    2428 1451
                                                                  2428 1451
       G.P.A. Nobre, M.T. Pigni, D.A. Brown, R. Capote, A. Trkov, 2428 1451
 K.H. Guber, R. Arcilla, J. Gutierrez, A. Cuadra, G. Arbanas      2428 1451
                                                                  2428 1451
                                                                  2428 1451
Fast region:                                                      2428 1451
                                                                  2428 1451
Due to the non-existence of experimental data for 51Cr, above     2428 1451
the inelastic threshold we adopted calculations from the nuclear  2428 1451
reaction model code EMPIRE-3.2.3 Malta (SVN rev.  5170; source    2428 1451
rev.  5168), using a parametrization based on the the one used    2428 1451
for 53Cr for this same set of chromium evaluations. That means    2428 1451
we also performed coupled-channel calculations using an           2428 1451
interpolated version of the dispersive soft-rotor optical         2428 1451
potential of Li et al. (RIPL #616), but assuming a rigid rotor,   2428 1451
labeled as RIPL #617. Fast capture was normalized to match        2428 1451
ENDF/B-VIII.0 at the inelastic threshold and preequilibirum was   2428 1451
adjusted to be around 1b at 14.1 MeV.                             2428 1451
                                                                  2428 1451
                                                                  2428 1451
Resolved Resonance Region:                                        2428 1451
                                                                  2428 1451
There are no data in the resonance region for 51Cr either,        2428 1451
so we simply adopted ENDF/B-VIII.0 below the inelastic            2428 1451
threshold:                                                        2428 1451
                      Resonance Range                             2428 1451
                                                                  2428 1451
  --------------------------------------------------------------- 2428 1451
  --------------------------------------------------------------- 2428 1451
                                                                  2428 1451
  General methodology: The global approach considered in this     2428 1451
          work is presented in the following paper: Modern        2428 1451
          nuclear data evaluation with the TALYS code system,     2428 1451
          A.J. Koning and D. Rochman, Nuclear Data Sheets 113     2428 1451
          (2012) 2841.                                            2428 1451
                                                                  2428 1451
  MF2:  Resolved resonance range  (RRR)                           2428 1451
       The RRR was generated with TARES-1.31, compiled on         2428 1451
       12-10-2015 11:58:11 PM at Villingen  , Switzerland. The RRR2428 1451
       expands from 0 to 5.096834E+4 eV. A total of               2428 1451
       2 l-values are used and 54 resonances. The resonance       2428 1451
       formalism is multi-level Breit Wigner (MLBW).              2428 1451
       The ladder approach from the CALENDF code is used to       2428 1451
       generate statistical resonances in the unresolved          2428 1451
       resonance range. Therefore, the URR is translated into     2428 1451
       resolved resonance range. Explanations about the method    2428 1451
       can be found in the CALENDF manual: CEA-Report CEA-R-6277  2428 1451
       "CALENDF-2010: User manual" by J.C. Sublet, P. Ribon and   2428 1451
       M. Coste-Delcaux.                                          2428 1451
       The method of creating statistical resonances in the       2428 1451
       URR region is described in: "From average parameters to    2428 1451
       statistical resolved resonances", D. Rochman et al.,       2428 1451
       Annals of Nucl. Ene. 51 (2013) 60.                         2428 1451
       The s-wave average level spacing is 747 eV and             2428 1451
       the s-wave neutron strength is 0.0007002 1e-4.             2428 1451
